Package: RAMEN
Title: Dynamic Bipartite Additive and Multiplicative Effects Models
Version: 2.0.0
Authors@R: person("Jing", "Luo", email = "luo.1405@osu.edu", role = c("aut", "cre"))
Description: Implements dynamic additive and multiplicative effects (AME)
    models for bipartite network data. Sender and receiver additive effects,
    regression coefficients, and latent factors each follow a Gaussian random
    walk, and all five parameter trajectories are estimated jointly across the
    whole panel by block coordinate descent on the penalized maximum a
    posteriori objective, solving the block-tridiagonal system that the
    random-walk prior induces for each block. The eleven variance components
    are estimated by empirical Bayes rather than supplied as tuning constants,
    and the penalties are derived from them. Supports row, column, and dyadic
    covariates, unbalanced panels with missing dyads, multi-start
    initialization, and two parametric bootstrap designs for inference. The
    earlier period-by-period alternating least squares functions are retained
    but deprecated.
